---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy | Odal Node";
const description =
  "How the Odal Node websites handle your data: no cookies, no analytics, no third-party trackers. Who is responsible, what the host sees, what happens to an email you send, and your rights.";

// This policy covers both websites, odal-node.io and docs.odal-node.io. Both
// are static sites with no backend. How the Odal Node software handles product
// data is a separate, architectural question; see /trust.
//
// GDPR Art. 13 is the checklist this page follows: who the controller is and
// how to reach them (13(1)(a)), each purpose with its legal basis (13(1)(c)),
// recipients (13(1)(e)), transfers outside the EU (13(1)(f)), how long data is
// kept (13(2)(a)), the rights including objection, which Art. 21(4) says must
// be shown separately (13(2)(b)), consent withdrawal (13(2)(c)), complaint
// (13(2)(d)), whether giving data is required (13(2)(e)) and automated
// decisions (13(2)(f)).
//
// 🔒 Name the controller and the mailbox, never a location: a name and a way
// to reach them are what 13(1)(a) asks for. Do not add a country, city or
// address here or anywhere public. When the company is registered it becomes
// the controller: put its registered name here instead.
const CONTROLLER = "Aleksandar Temelkov";
const MAILBOX = "contact@odal-node.io";

const updated = "2026-09-29";
const updatedText = new Date(`${updated}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
  day: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
});
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Section h1 eyebrow="Privacy Policy" title="No cookies, no analytics, no trackers.">
    <p>
      This policy covers both Odal Node websites: this one and the
      documentation site.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The sites set <strong>no cookies</strong>.</li>
      <li>There is <strong>no analytics</strong>: no Google Analytics, Plausible, Fathom, or any equivalent.</li>
      <li>There are <strong>no third-party trackers, advertising pixels, or social embeds</strong>.</li>
      <li>We do not build a profile of you, and we do not sell or share data.</li>
      <li>The only personal data involved is what your browser sends to load a page, and anything you choose to email us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600">
      Last updated <time datetime={updated}>{updatedText}</time>.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Who is responsible" title="Who looks after your data." tone="tinted">
    <p>
      Odal Node is run by <strong>{CONTROLLER}</strong>, who is responsible
      for these websites and for the personal data described on this page
      (the "controller" under the GDPR). Odal Node is not a registered company
      yet. When it is, the company takes over this role and is named here.
    </p>
    <p>
      For anything about your data, write to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${MAILBOX}`}>{MAILBOX}</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Hosting" title="What the host sees.">
    <p>
      Both sites are served as static files by <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong>.
      As with any website, your browser must connect to a server to load a page,
      and that connection is visible to the host. Cloudflare processes standard
      request data: your <strong>IP address</strong>, the time of the request,
      the page requested, your browser's user-agent string, and similar
      technical details.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is needed to deliver the pages and to protect them from abuse, such
      as attacks that try to overload them. Our legal basis is our legitimate
      interest in serving and securing the sites (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)). We do
      not run analytics over this data and do not receive it as a record of you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare processes this data on our behalf as our hosting provider,
      under its data processing terms. How long it keeps its logs is set out in{" "}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      Cloudflare may process the data in the United States. It is certified
      under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, which the European Commission has
      found to protect personal data adequately (Implementing Decision (EU)
      2023/1795).
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Email" title="What happens to an email you send us." tone="tinted">
    <p>
      If you write to us, for example to join the waitlist, we receive your
      email address, your name if you give it, and whatever your message says.
      Writing to us is up to you. Without your email we cannot reply.
    </p>
    <p>We use it for two things:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>To reply to you.</strong> The legal basis is our legitimate
        interest in answering the people who write to us, or, when you ask
        about using Odal Node, taking the steps you asked for before any
        agreement (GDPR Article 6(1)(f) and 6(1)(b)).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To write to you later</strong> when something you asked about
        is ready, such as your product group. We do this only if you ask us to,
        and that request is your consent (Article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it
        at any time by telling us, and we stop.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not add you to a mailing list. Nobody but us and the provider that
      hosts our email handles what you send. That provider processes it on our
      behalf and may do so in the United States, under the EU-US Data Privacy
      Framework.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep your emails for two years after our last exchange, then delete
      them. If you ask us to delete them sooner, we do.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Your browser" title="What stays on your device.">
    <p>
      The documentation site remembers whether you chose a light or dark
      display, in your browser's local storage. It is never sent to us, and
      you can clear it in your browser's settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      The documentation's API reference can send a test request to a node
      address you enter. That request goes straight from your browser to that
      address. It does not pass through us.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Off-site links" title="Where the sites send you." tone="tinted">
    <p>
      Some links lead to other websites: our{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/odal-node" rel="noopener">GitHub organisation</a>,
      the official texts of EU law, and a few cited standards. Once you follow
      them you are on someone else's website, governed by its own privacy
      practices, not this one. We have no control over what those services
      collect.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Your rights" title="What you can ask of us.">
    <p>Under the GDPR you can ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>tell you what personal data we hold about you, and give you a copy;</li>
      <li>correct it;</li>
      <li>delete it;</li>
      <li>limit how we use it while a question about it is settled;</li>
      <li>send it to you, or to someone you name, in a common format.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Your right to object.</strong> Where we use your data on the basis
      of our legitimate interest, you can object at any time, for reasons
      relating to your situation. We then stop, unless we have compelling
      legitimate grounds that override your interests, rights and freedoms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where we rely on your consent, you can withdraw it at any time. This does
      not affect what we did before you withdrew it.
    </p>
    <p>
      To use any of these rights, write to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${MAILBOX}`}>{MAILBOX}</a>. We reply within one month.
      Because the only personal data we hold is what you have emailed us, a
      request usually means "delete our correspondence", which we will do.
    </p>
    <p>
      You also have the right to complain to a data protection authority, in
      particular in the EU country where you live or work, or where you think
      the problem arose.
    </p>
    <p>We make no automated decisions about you and do not profile you.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Changes" title="How this page changes." tone="tinted">
    <p>
      Changes to this policy are made in public. The websites' source, with
      every earlier version of this page, is in its{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/odal-node/dpp-web" rel="noopener">public repository</a>.
      For who runs Odal Node and what the information on these sites is and is
      not, see the <a href="/legal">legal notice</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>
